// merge_section.dg — generic left-join: for each row in `collectedRows` (each a Map with an
// `idField` key), find the matching entry in `writtenRows` (Claude's structured output for that
// section, or null for profiles/sections with no LLM call) and merge the written fields onto the
// collected ones. This is the implementation of what the original single-user prototype left as
// an unimplemented `mergeCollectedAndWritten` TODO. Reused by every profile's generator.
//
// Returns a JSON-stringified List — Standalone category functions can only declare return type
// string (and only accept string/int/date/float/bool/map as argument types — not List —
// confirmed by a live "Invalid Argument Type List" error); callers pass `.toString()` of their
// Lists (writtenRowsJson may be null/empty when a section had no LLM output) and parse the
// result back with `.toJSONList()` immediately at the call site.

string standalone.mergeSection(String collectedRowsJson, String writtenRowsJson, String idField)
{
	collectedRows = collectedRowsJson.toJSONList();
	writtenById = Map();
	if (writtenRowsJson != null && writtenRowsJson != "") {
		writtenRows = writtenRowsJson.toJSONList();
		for each w in writtenRows { writtenById.put(w.get(idField), w); }
	}

	merged = List();
	for each c in collectedRows {
		row = Map();
		row.putAll(c);
		written = writtenById.get(c.get(idField));
		if (written != null) { row.putAll(written); }
		merged.add(row);
	}
	return merged.toString();
}
